{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Laban said, etc. — ״Are you truly my brother, etc.״</b> It is difficult: who told him that he was serving him for nothing? And further, even if it be as his words — so what if he serves him for nothing? And if his intention is to say that he is one who ״hates gifts shall live״ (Proverbs 15:27) — but have we not found that he loves robbery, and all the more so that he would desire to receive what is given willingly!" "<b>Truly,</b> his lips clearly articulate that he came only to diminish Jacob's wage, and this is along the lines of what the Rambam wrote (Laws of Agents and Partners, chapter 6 and chapter 8) that any shepherd who did not stipulate with the owner takes his wage from the deposit's portion at one third of the profit, and for calves and colts two thirds. Therefore Laban was concerned, for Jacob's reasoning was that he did not make it explicit that his intent was to take one third of the grown animals and two thirds of the calves, etc. And the deceiver trembled at the matter — and it is true, if Jacob had been like one of the fools, he would not have been insistent that he intended this, and then either he would give his mind afterward, and Laban would turn a blind eye to him and have him work for nothing; but because of what preceded — that Jacob had made known that he too would deal craftily with the cunning man — therefore he wished to reveal it, and that is his saying <b>״Are you truly my brother?״</b> — as cunning as I am, in the manner of the verse's saying (Genesis 29:12) ״he is her father's brother,״ and as became known to him from the deeds that Jacob recounted to him. <b>״And will you serve me for nothing?״</b> — meaning, is it to be believed that you will serve for nothing? Surely you will come with a claim in the end and take what is fitting to take by law; therefore I want you to reveal your mind: ״Tell me,״ etc. — and any condition involving money is binding."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:41.746983026Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}